{
  "summary": "This experiment tested an RNA-only model with multiprofile and avgpool aggregation, achieving 59.07% validation accuracy and 57.27% F1. The result suggests multiprofile and avgpool may contribute to performance gains compared to singleprofile baselines, but the absence of image modality in this configuration limits conclusions about their isolated impact. Uncertainty remains about the relative effectiveness of aggregation methods and the potential role of profile settings without multimodal interactions."
}

